shed the lead from +6.7 to +13.7. Black's F-file wall (F6, F5, F4, F3) was already standing, and White's stones on E4 and E5 sat on the wrong side of it. After this the lead stayed above 12 for the rest of the game."}, {"turn": 26, "text": "J3 was the sixth straight Opus 5.5 move to lose 6.7 points or more, this one 7.0. It built up the White group on H3, H2 and G2. Black's G1 reply lost 7.0 as well, but Black stayed far enough ahead that it did not matter."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py and count.py only parse a pasted board and compute groups, liberties and area/territory of the current position, and the games.md commands just read and append notes; nothing chooses, ranks or looks ahead at moves.", "stop": false}}